  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "i/kE6S8NEyhTKcMlgNoMRCRJZKA=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:36:30.075Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Walking a drive from a resolver\n\nA custom subgraph that searches or aggregates across a drive needs the drive's contents. In v6 that is a relationship query on the reactor client, not a walk over a `nodes` array:\n\n```ts\nexport const getResolvers = (subgraph: BaseSubgraph) => {\n  const reactorClient = subgraph.reactorClient;\n\n  return {\n    Query: {\n      searchTodos: async (\n        parent: unknown,\n        args: { driveId: string; searchTerm: string },\n      ) => {\n        const children = await reactorClient.getOutgoingRelationships(\n          args.driveId,\n          \"child\",\n        );\n        const todoItems: string[] = [];\n        for (const doc of children.results) {\n          if (doc.header.documentType !== \"powerhouse/todo-list\") continue;\n          const todoDoc = doc as TodoListDocument;\n          const hits = todoDoc.state.global.items.filter((e) =>\n            e.text.includes(args.searchTerm),\n          ).length;\n          if (hits > 0) todoItems.push(doc.header.id);\n        }\n        return todoItems;\n      },\n    },\n  };\n};\n```\n\nThree details to carry over into your own resolvers:\n\n- **`\"child\"` is the relationship type.** Drive membership is modelled as an outgoing relationship from the drive document, which is why the same call generalises to any relationship you define.\n- **Results come back as a page**, read via `children.results` \u2014 not a bare array. Large drives require paging, so a resolver that assumes one page is correct only by accident.\n- **Type filtering is yours to do.** The call returns documents of every type in the drive; each carries `header.documentType`, and skipping the ones you do not care about is resolver code, not a query parameter.\n\nThe same `getOutgoingRelationships` call backs the built-in reactor resolvers, so this is the supported path rather than a workaround.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/04-WorkWithData/03-UsingSubgraphs.md, packages/reactor-api/src/graphql/reactor/resolvers.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:36:29.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:36:30.075Z"
    }
  },
